# Network games at a higher resolution: a client is sent the host's screen with every area and
# widget rect already scaled, and adds them with Display::add_area / add_item, which the patcher's
# resolution change hooks to scale from 800x600: the client scaled them twice (1.75 times too big
# at 1680x1050). The client's packet handler (0x564080) now calls add_area / add_item past that
# hook (stubs in .nick at 0xdf2000 / 0xdf2010 run the hook's moved instruction only). Where the
# exe has the bigger-fonts step (jmp at 0x55fa14) the client's font is taken one down first, as
# the host stepped it already. Only the client's packet handler changes: host and single player
# untouched; on an exe without the resolution change the stubs do what the game did.
